# Fénix Definition Language (FDL) Example
# Booking Automation System for Small Clinics

product BookingAutomation

vision
    Automate the reservation process for small clinics, eliminating manual phone calls
    and reducing no-shows by 40%. The system will provide a modern web interface for
    patients to book appointments 24/7, with automatic SMS reminders and integration
    with existing clinic management systems.

users
    Administrator
        Manages clinic settings, providers, and schedules
        Can override bookings and generate reports

    Provider
        Doctor or healthcare provider
        Manages their own availability and appointments
        Can accept/reject patient requests

    Customer
        Patient looking to book appointments
        Can view available slots and book appointments
        Receives SMS reminders

constraints
    OAuth2
        AzureAD integration for staff authentication

    GDPR
        All patient data must be encrypted at rest
        Audit logs for all data access
        Right to be forgotten implementation

    HIPAA
        PHI must be stored in compliant database
        Access controls by role
        Breach notification procedures

    MaxLatency: 200ms
        API responses must be under 200ms for critical operations

    Availability: 99.9%
        System uptime SLA

feature Authentication
    story UserLogin
        requirement
            Users authenticate using Azure AD OAuth2
            Sessions expire after 15 minutes of inactivity
            Password reset via email verification
            Multi-factor authentication for administrators
        acceptance
            Given a valid Azure AD token
            When the user attempts to login
            Then the system issues a JWT and redirects to Dashboard
            And the JWT contains user role and permissions
        architecture
            API
                AuthenticationService
                    Handles OAuth2 flow
                    Issues JWT tokens
                    Validates sessions
                JwtProvider
                    Generates and validates JWTs
                    Handles token refresh
                UserRepository
                    Stores user profiles and roles
                AuditLogger
                    Logs all authentication events
        tests
            Integration: Verify AzureAD handshake
            Unit: JWT decoding and validation
            Security: Test session expiration
            Security: Test MFA flow

    story PasswordReset
        requirement
            Users can request password reset via email
            Reset links expire after 1 hour
            New passwords must meet complexity requirements
        acceptance
            Given a user requests password reset
            When they click the email link
            Then they can set a new password
            And the old password is immediately invalidated
        architecture
            API
                PasswordResetService
                    Generates reset tokens
                    Validates reset links
                    Updates passwords
            EmailService
                Sends reset emails
            SecurityService
                Enforces password complexity
        tests
            Unit: Token generation and validation
            Integration: Email delivery
            Security: Token expiration

feature Scheduling
    story BookAppointment
        requirement
            Customer selects an available time slot
            Slot must be locked for 5 minutes during checkout
            Customer provides reason for visit
            Insurance information collected if applicable
        acceptance
            Given a customer views available slots
            When they select a slot and confirm booking
            Then the slot is reserved for 5 minutes
            And they must complete checkout within 5 minutes
            And upon completion, they receive confirmation SMS
        architecture
            Database
                PostgreSQL (Isolation Level: Serializable)
                    Stores appointments with row-level locking
                    Enforces slot uniqueness
            Cache
                Redis (Distributed Lock)
                    Manages slot reservations
                    Handles 5-minute timeout
            API
                BookingService
                    Creates reservation
                    Handles checkout flow
                SmsService
                    Sends confirmation SMS
        tests
            Integration: PostgreSQL locking
            Integration: Redis distributed lock
            Unit: Checkout timeout logic
            Load: Test concurrent booking attempts

    story ManageAvailability
        requirement
            Providers can set recurring availability
            Providers can block specific time ranges
            Providers can set maximum daily appointments
        acceptance
            Given a provider wants to set availability
            When they configure their schedule
            Then the system stores their recurring patterns
            And they can override specific dates
        architecture
            Database
                PostgreSQL
                    Stores availability patterns
                    Stores exceptions and overrides
            API
                AvailabilityService
                    Manages recurring patterns
                    Handles exceptions
                CalendarService
                    Generates available slots from patterns
        tests
            Unit: Pattern generation logic
            Integration: Override handling
            Unit: Slot generation algorithm

feature Notifications
    story AppointmentReminders
        requirement
            Send SMS reminder 24 hours before appointment
            Send SMS reminder 2 hours before appointment
            Allow patients to cancel via SMS reply
        acceptance
            Given an appointment is scheduled
            When the appointment time approaches
            Then the system sends SMS reminders
            And patients can reply CANCEL to cancel
        architecture
            External Services
                Twilio API
                    Sends SMS messages
                    Handles inbound replies
            Background Services
                ReminderWorker
                    Scans for upcoming appointments
                    Queues SMS sends
            API
                NotificationService
                    Manages notification preferences
                    Tracks delivery status
        tests
            Integration: Twilio API
            Unit: Reminder scheduling logic
            Unit: Reply parsing

feature Reporting
    story GenerateReports
        requirement
            Administrators can generate appointment reports
            Reports can be filtered by date range, provider, status
            Reports exportable to CSV and PDF
        acceptance
            Given an administrator wants reports
            When they select filters and generate
            Then the system aggregates appointment data
            And exports in requested format
        architecture
            Database
                PostgreSQL
                    Optimized queries for reporting
                    Materialized views for common reports
            API
                ReportService
                    Generates report queries
                    Handles export formats
                FileService
                    Stores generated reports
        tests
            Integration: Report query performance
            Unit: CSV export generation
            Unit: PDF export generation

feature Integrations
    story EHRIntegration
        requirement
            Sync appointment data with external EHR systems
            Support HL7 FHIR standard
            Handle bi-directional sync
        acceptance
            Given an appointment is created
            When the sync process runs
            Then the data is sent to the EHR system
            And any changes in EHR are reflected in Fénix
        architecture
            External Services
                EHR API (FHIR-compliant)
                    Receives appointment data
                    Provides patient demographics
            Background Services
                SyncWorker
                    Processes outbound sync
                    Polls for inbound changes
            API
                IntegrationService
                    Maps data to FHIR format
                    Handles retry logic
        tests
            Integration: FHIR mapping
            Integration: Retry logic
            Unit: Change detection

implementation
    Backend
        Language: Go 1.22+
        Framework: Chi router
        Database: PostgreSQL 15
        Cache: Redis 7
        Message Queue: RabbitMQ (for background jobs)

    Frontend
        Framework: React 18
        Meta-framework: Next.js 14
        UI Library: shadcn/ui
        State Management: Zustand
        Forms: React Hook Form

    Mobile
        Framework: Flutter 3
        State: Riverpod
        Navigation: GoRouter

    Infrastructure
        Hosting: AWS
        Compute: ECS Fargate
        Database: RDS PostgreSQL
        Cache: ElastiCache Redis
        CDN: CloudFront
        Monitoring: Datadog

release
    v1.0
        scope
            MVP with core features
            Authentication (Azure AD)
            Scheduling (book, manage availability)
            Basic notifications (SMS reminders)
            Simple reporting

    v1.1
        scope
            Enhanced reporting
            EHR integration (single provider)
            Mobile app (iOS only)

    v2.0
        scope
            Multi-tenant support
            Advanced EHR integrations
            Mobile app (Android)
            Telehealth integration
